There are absolute constants \(a_*\in(0,1/2)\) and \(C_*<\infty\) such that every Lipschitz field \(v:\R^2	o S^1\) with \(\Lip(v)\le1\) satisfies \[ \sup_{0<\epsilon<a_*} 
orm{H_{v,a_*}^{\epsilon}f}_{L^2(\R^2)} \le C_*
orm{f}_{L^2(\R^2)} \qquad(f\in\mathcal S(\R^2)). \] Its symmetric principal value therefore satisfies \[ 
orm{H_{v,a_*}f}_2\le C_*
orm f_2, \qquad  ig|\{x:|H_{v,a_*}f(x)|>\lambda\} ig| \le C_*^2\lambda^{-2}
orm f_2^2 \quad(\lambda>0). \]
